# Planning a method: the three steps only work in one order, and nothing on the page says which.
item chem.sand-salt-steps v=1 stars=3 skills=[chemistry.separating, reasoning.plan] {
  title "Getting both back"
  difficulty o
  let o=0..5

  scene 29x14 {
    text ask "Sand and salt are mixed together, dry. Number the steps in the order that gets both back on their own." width=28 at=canvas(1, 0)
    mixture mix things=["sand", "salt"] water=0 names=1 below=ask gap=0
    sequence s items=["{if o == 0 then \"Add water and stir\" else if o == 1 then \"Add water and stir\" else if o == 2 then \"Pour it through filter paper\" else if o == 3 then \"Pour it through filter paper\" else if o == 4 then \"Leave the water to evaporate\" else \"Leave the water to evaporate\"}", "{if o == 0 then \"Pour it through filter paper\" else if o == 1 then \"Leave the water to evaporate\" else if o == 2 then \"Add water and stir\" else if o == 3 then \"Leave the water to evaporate\" else if o == 4 then \"Add water and stir\" else \"Pour it through filter paper\"}", "{if o == 0 then \"Leave the water to evaporate\" else if o == 1 then \"Pour it through filter paper\" else if o == 2 then \"Leave the water to evaporate\" else if o == 3 then \"Add water and stir\" else if o == 4 then \"Pour it through filter paper\" else \"Add water and stir\"}"] blanks=[a, b, c] right-of=mix gap=1
  }

  answer a=(if o == 0 then 1 else if o == 1 then 1 else if o == 2 then 2 else if o == 3 then 2 else if o == 4 then 3 else 3) b=(if o == 0 then 2 else if o == 1 then 3 else if o == 2 then 1 else if o == 3 then 3 else if o == 4 then 1 else 2) c=(if o == 0 then 3 else if o == 1 then 2 else if o == 2 then 3 else if o == 3 then 1 else if o == 4 then 2 else 1)
  hint "The sand and the salt are both grains. Which way could tell them apart once one of them has dissolved?"
  hint "What has to happen before filter paper can be any use?"
  hint "After filtering, where is the salt, and how would you get it out of there?"
}
